# CRYSS Project

CRYSS (Crystallisation Research & Yield Simulation Suite) is an open-source
project focused on modelling, analysing, and visualising crystallisation
behaviour. The project includes tools for simulation, data processing, and
experimental workflow support.

This repository contains the source code, documentation, and downloadable
artifacts for the CRYSS project. All components are released under the MIT
License to support academic, industrial, and commercial use.

## Features

- Crystallisation modelling and simulation tools  
- Data processing utilities  
- Visualisation components  
- Experimental workflow helpers  
- MIT-licensed source code and binaries  
- Public GitHub Pages site for documentation

## Website

The project website is available at:

**https://cryss.co.uk**

This site is hosted using GitHub Pages and contains documentation, downloads,
and project updates.

## Downloads

Compiled binaries, datasets, and other artifacts are available under the
**Releases** section of this repository:

https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo>/releases

